{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FihGheReug3bW2uoGpDYuE","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, **no**, the dedicated configuration to cap the maximum size of headers was **not** kept in the final design as of mid-January 2026.\\\\n\\\\nHere's what happened:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Initial proposal (January 9)**: The original KIP-1271 proposal introduced \\\\\\\"a small config to cap the size of headers written into state\\\\\\\" (referred to as `streams.store.headers.max.bytes`).\\\\n\\\\n2. **Feedback (January 12)**: Matthias J. Sax questioned this configuration in his review, asking why a limit on header size was needed at all, since Kafka Streams doesn't limit key or value sizes, and Kafka's message size limits already implicitly cover headers.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Design change (January 14)**: Alieh Saeedi updated the KIP to **remove the configuration**, stating explicitly:\\\\n   > \\\\\\\"I have removed the two-byte header size and its associated configuration property. Since we are using varints for the header count, as well as for individual key and value sizes within each header, a global 'headers size' field is redundant and could be restrictive.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n4. **Later refinement (January 16)**: Instead of the configuration, a **varint header_size field** was introduced (not a configuration, but a serialized field) to enable lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges of records.\\\\n\\\\n**Sources:**\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1271/2026-01-12-mail-discuss-state-store-headers-8e225897.md` (Matthias's question about the config)\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1271/2026-01-14-mail-1c0b316b9c6624add1f97d07-4afb9253.md` (Alieh's confirmation of the removal)\\\\n- `/store/kips/KIP-1271/2026-01-27-mail-discuss-state-store-headers-5f8c2a1e.md` (Later discussion confirming the varint field)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"INDEX.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1271\\\",\\\"